# CRITICAL GIT DEPLOYMENT & REPOSITORY SYNC RULES

===============================================================================
WARNING — READ THIS FILE BEFORE ANY GIT ACTION
===============================================================================

This file is the AUTHORITATIVE Git deployment and repository synchronization
rule for the project.

Before running ANY of the following commands:

- git add
- git commit
- git push
- git pull
- git checkout
- git branch
- git merge
- git subtree
- any repository synchronization command

YOU MUST READ AND FOLLOW THIS FILE.

NEVER make Git decisions based on assumptions.

===============================================================================
1. PROJECT STRUCTURE
===============================================================================

The project is maintained as a monorepo containing multiple project areas:

- backend/
- frontend/
- web-frontend/
- other project-level files

Each dedicated developer repository has a STRICT scope.

The central personal repository contains the COMPLETE project.

