===============================================================================
3. SIMPLE CHANGE → REPOSITORY RULE
===============================================================================

Use this exact mapping.

┌──────────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ Changed Project              │ Dedicated Repository                       │
├──────────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ backend/**                   │ Backend---NFC-QR-code-Management            │
│ frontend/**                  │ Frontend---NFC-QR-code-Management           │
│ web-frontend/**              │ Web-Frontend---NFC-QR-code-Management       │
│ Any project update           │ Personal NFC-QR-code central repository     │
└──────────────────────────────┴──────────────────────────────────────────────┘

IMPORTANT:

Every legitimate project change must go to the CENTRAL PERSONAL REPOSITORY.

Additionally:

- Backend changes → Backend dedicated repository
- React Native changes → Frontend dedicated repository
- Web Frontend changes → Web Frontend dedicated repository

===============================================================================
4. MULTI-PROJECT CHANGE RULE
===============================================================================

If a single task modifies multiple project areas, push each scope separately.

Example:

If a task changes:

backend/src/routes.ts
web-frontend/src/pages/BartenderPage.tsx

Then:

CENTRAL REPOSITORY:
    Push both changes.

BACKEND REPOSITORY:
    Push ONLY backend changes.

WEB FRONTEND REPOSITORY:
    Push ONLY web-frontend changes.

DO NOT mix them inside dedicated repositories.

===============================================================================
5. BARTENDER PAGE EXAMPLE
===============================================================================

For the Bartender Page workflow implementation:

If the changes are:

backend/src/services/RedemptionService.ts
backend/src/routes.ts

web-frontend/src/pages/BartenderPage.tsx
web-frontend/src/services/api.ts
web-frontend/src/pages/TablesPage.tsx

Then:

CENTRAL PERSONAL REPOSITORY:
    Push ALL of the above changes.

BACKEND REPOSITORY:
    Push ONLY:
        backend/src/services/RedemptionService.ts
        backend/src/routes.ts

WEB FRONTEND REPOSITORY:
    Push ONLY:
        web-frontend/src/pages/BartenderPage.tsx
        web-frontend/src/services/api.ts
        web-frontend/src/pages/TablesPage.tsx

REACT NATIVE FRONTEND REPOSITORY:
    Push NOTHING unless frontend/ was actually modified.

===============================================================================
6. DO NOT PUSH UNRELATED PROJECTS
===============================================================================

NEVER do this:

git add .

inside a dedicated repository context if it can stage files from unrelated
project scopes.

Before committing to a dedicated repository, verify the staged files.

For Web Frontend repository:

EVERY staged file must belong to web-frontend scope.

For Backend repository:

EVERY staged file must belong to backend scope.

For React Native repository:

EVERY staged file must belong to frontend scope.

If an unrelated path appears:

STOP.

Unstage it.

Correct the repository scope.

Only then continue.

===============================================================================
7. ROOT-LEVEL REQUIREMENT FOR DEDICATED REPOSITORIES
===============================================================================

Dedicated repositories must NOT contain the monorepo parent folder.

The following structure is REQUIRED:

Dedicated Repo
├── src/
├── package.json
├── config files
└── other project files

NOT:

Dedicated Repo
└── web-frontend/
    └── src/

NOT:

Dedicated Repo
└── backend/
    └── src/

NOT:

Dedicated Repo
└── frontend/
    └── src/

The dedicated repository represents the project itself.

Therefore its project files must exist directly at repository root.

===============================================================================
8. GIT PRE-FLIGHT CHECK — MANDATORY
===============================================================================

BEFORE EVERY COMMIT OR PUSH:

STEP 1:
Check the current repository.

Verify:

- current directory
- git root
- current branch
- configured remotes

STEP 2:
Run:

git status

STEP 3:
Inspect tracked files:

git ls-files

STEP 4:
Inspect the exact staged files:

git diff --cached --name-only

STEP 5:
Verify the remote URL.

The remote MUST correspond to the intended repository.

STEP 6:
Verify branch.

CENTRAL:
    main

WEB FRONTEND:
    webfrontend-branch

BACKEND:
    appropriate existing deployment branch after verification

REACT NATIVE FRONTEND:
    appropriate existing deployment branch after verification

DO NOT create branches unless explicitly permitted by these rules.

===============================================================================
9. WEB FRONTEND — EXTRA STRICT RULE
===============================================================================

The Web Frontend repository is exclusively for:

web-frontend/

NEVER treat the monorepo root as the Web Frontend repository scope.

Before every Web Frontend commit/push:

1. Verify only Web Frontend files are being synchronized.
2. Verify backend files are absent.
3. Verify React Native files are absent.
4. Verify database/unrelated files are absent.
5. Verify the dedicated branch:
   webfrontend-branch
6. Verify the resulting repository has Web Frontend files at ROOT level.

If ANY unrelated file is staged:

STOP THE OPERATION.

Do not bypass this rule.

===============================================================================
10. BACKEND — STRICT RULE
===============================================================================

The Backend repository is exclusively for:

backend/

Only backend project contents may be synchronized.

If there are no backend changes:

DO NOT push to the Backend repository.

===============================================================================
11. REACT NATIVE FRONTEND — STRICT RULE
===============================================================================

The React Native Frontend repository is exclusively for:

frontend/

