===============================================================================
13. NEVER MIX DEDICATED REPOSITORIES
===============================================================================

NEVER:

- Push backend into Web Frontend repo.
- Push backend into React Native repo.
- Push Web Frontend into Backend repo.
- Push React Native into Web Frontend repo.
- Push the entire monorepo into a dedicated repository.
- Create nested backend/frontend/web-frontend wrappers inside dedicated repos.

===============================================================================
14. NO ASSUMPTIONS
===============================================================================

Before any Git operation, inspect the actual repository state.

Do NOT assume:

- current branch
- remote URL
- repository root
- subtree branch state
- existing tracked files
- existing branch names

Verify them first.

If the actual repository state conflicts with this document:

STOP and report the conflict before performing a destructive or irreversible
Git operation.

===============================================================================
15. EAS / EIS RULE
===============================================================================

EAS/EIS commands must ONLY be executed inside:

frontend/

or the exact React Native project directory containing:

eas.json

Never run EAS/EIS commands from:

- monorepo root
- backend/
- web-frontend/

===============================================================================
16. RECENT PROJECT REPOSITORY RULE
===============================================================================

The project previously established the following repository-cleanup principles:

- Dedicated repositories must remain lightweight.
- Non-runtime project logs/notepads should not be accidentally pushed.
- Unrelated folders must remain excluded from dedicated repositories.
- `.gitignore` rules should prevent accidental tracking where applicable.

Do not reintroduce removed unrelated files into dedicated repositories.

===============================================================================
17. FINAL DECISION MATRIX
===============================================================================

When deciding where to push a change, use this exact decision process:

IF file is under:

backend/
    → Central repository
    → Backend dedicated repository

frontend/
    → Central repository
    → React Native Frontend dedicated repository

web-frontend/
    → Central repository
    → Web Frontend dedicated repository

IF file belongs to project root or another legitimate project scope:

    → Central repository ONLY

IF a dedicated repository has no changes in its project scope:

    → DO NOT PUSH to that dedicated repository.

===============================================================================
18. FINAL SAFETY RULE
===============================================================================

The CENTRAL repository receives ALL project updates.

The DEDICATED repositories receive ONLY their respective project updates.

Therefore:

CENTRAL:
    COMPLETE PROJECT

BACKEND:
    backend/ ONLY

REACT NATIVE FRONTEND:
    frontend/ ONLY

WEB FRONTEND:
    web-frontend/ ONLY

This rule is mandatory and overrides convenience, automatic Git
synchronization, bulk staging, and bulk repository operations.

